  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_012, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. All top-performing configs share the same image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and the only other image encoder (resnet50) has not been tested with the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200) and transformer aggregation. The RNA encoder choice has shown to be the dominant factor (scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 >> scgpt), and aggregation/fusion choices are well-characterized (transformer > avgpool, weighted ≈ concat). Question: Does the image encoder architecture matter when paired with the best RNA encoder and transformer aggregation? Config_019 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) directly isolates this variable. If resnet50 performs comparably (~0.70+), it confirms the image encoder is less critical and saves compute for remaining experiments; if it drops significantly, it validates imagenet_vit_l as essential and focuses remaining budget on other refinements. Expected cost: ResNet50 is smaller than ViT-L, so this should be moderately cheaper than config_012 (3.60 hrs), estimated ~2.5–3.5 GPU hours, making it a cost-effective exploration of the last major untested architectural axis."
}

